(1)  989/       0 :                     ; The original SMPS2ASM decides TL high bits automatically,
(1)  990/       0 :                     ; but later versions leave it up to the user.
(1)  991/       0 :                     ; Alternatively, if we're converting an SMPS 68k song to SMPS Z80,
(1)  992/       0 :                     ; then we *want* the TL bits to match the algorithm, because SMPS 68k
(1)  993/       0 :                     ; prefers the algorithm over the TL bits, ignoring the latter, while
(1)  994/       0 :                     ; SMPS Z80 does the opposite.
(1)  995/       0 :                     ; Unfortunately, there's nothing we can do if we're trying to convert
(1)  996/       0 :                     ; an SMPS Z80 song to SMPS 68k. It will ignore the bits no matter
(1)  997/       0 :                     ; what we do, so we just print a warning.
