    8641/    6446 :                     
    8642/    6446 :                     ; ===========================================================================
    8643/    6446 :                     ; pointers to the mappings for each frame of the special stage track
    8644/    6446 :                     ; indexed into by the numbers used in the above animations
    8645/    6446 :                     ;
    8646/    6446 :                     ; Format of each mappings file:
    8647/    6446 :                     ;	File is divided in 3 segments, with the same structure:
    8648/    6446 :                     ;	Segment structure:
    8649/    6446 :                     ;		4-byte unsigned length of segment (not counting the 4 bytes used for length);
    8650/    6446 :                     ;		the first 2 bytes of each length is ignored, and only the last 2 bytes are
    8651/    6446 :                     ;		actually used.
    8652/    6446 :                     ;		Rest of the segment is mappings data, as follows:
    8653/    6446 :                     ;	1st segment:
    8654/    6446 :                     ;		Mappings data is a bitstream indicating whether to draw a single tile at
    8655/    6446 :                     ;		a time using the uncompressed mappings (see 2nd segment) or a sequence of
    8656/    6446 :                     ;		tiles using the RLE mappings (see 3rd segment).
    8657/    6446 :                     ;	2nd segment:
    8658/    6446 :                     ;		Mappings data is a bitstream: the first bit in each cycle determines how
    8659/    6446 :                     ;		many bits from the stream are to be used as an index to the uncompressed
    8660/    6446 :                     ;		pattern name list SSPNT_UncLUT: if the first bit is set, 10 bits form an
    8661/    6446 :                     ;		index into SSPNT_UncLUT_Part2, otherwise 6 bits are used as an index into
    8662/    6446 :                     ;		SSPNT_UncLUT.
    8663/    6446 :                     ;		These tiles are drawn in palette line 3.
    8664/    6446 :                     ;	3nd segment:
    8665/    6446 :                     ;		Mappings data is a bitstream: the first bit in each cycle determines how
    8666/    6446 :                     ;		many bits from the stream are to be used as an index to the RLE-compressed
    8667/    6446 :                     ;		pattern name list SSPNT_RLELUT: if the first bit is set, 7 bits form an
    8668/    6446 :                     ;		index into SSPNT_RLELUT_Part2, otherwise 6 bits are used as an index into
    8669/    6446 :                     ;		SSPNT_RLELUT.
    8670/    6446 :                     ;		These tiles are drawn in palette line 3, with the high priority bit set.
