(1)   39/   2CFF8 :                     	; This check doesn't really work: it's possible for an object to be
(1)   40/   2CFF8 :                     	; loaded into the parent's slot before this object can check if the
(1)   41/   2CFF8 :                     	; slot is empty. In fact, it will always be immediately occupied by
(1)   42/   2CFF8 :                     	; the explosion object. This defect causes the flame to linger for a
(1)   43/   2CFF8 :                     	; while after the Buzzer is destroyed. A better way to do this check
(1)   44/   2CFF8 :                     	; would be to check if the ID is equal to 'ObjID_Buzzer'.
(1)   45/   2CFF8 : 4A11                	tst.b	id(a1)
(1)   46/   2CFFA : 6700 02D0           	beq.w	JmpTo49_DeleteObject	; branch, if object slot is empty. This check is incomplete and very unreliable; check Obj50_Wing to see how it should be done
