(1)  878/   2DFDA :                     	; If the Chemical Plant Zone boss is defeated while its pipe is
(1)  879/   2DFDA :                     	; extending, then an incorrect sprite will appear at the boss's rear
(1)  880/   2DFDA :                     	; as it explodes.
(1)  881/   2DFDA :                     	; Pipe segments are supposed to use sprite frame 1, but the
(1)  882/   2DFDA :                     	; AnimateSprite function must be called for that to happen. When the
(1)  883/   2DFDA :                     	; boss is defeated, the segment will switch from calling
(1)  884/   2DFDA :                     	; Obj5D_PipeSegment to Obj5D_PipeSegment_End, which does not call
(1)  885/   2DFDA :                     	; AnimateSprite.
(1)  886/   2DFDA :                     	; This means that if the boss were to be defeated right as a pipe
(1)  887/   2DFDA :                     	; segment spawns, then it will never call AnimateSprite, causing it to
(1)  888/   2DFDA :                     	; display sprite frame 0 instead of 1.
(1)  889/   2DFDA :                     	; To fix this bug, Obj5D_PipeSegment_End should be made to call
(1)  890/   2DFDA :                     	; AnimateSprite.
(1)  891/   2DFDA : (MACRO)              	jmpto	DisplaySprite, JmpTo34_DisplaySprite
(1)  891/   2DFDA : 6000 0E58                           !bra.w JmpTo34_DisplaySprite     ; otherwise, branch to an indirect JmpTo
