(1)  596/     14C :                     	; Tempo works as divisions of the 60Hz clock (there is a fix supplied for
(1)  597/     14C :                     	; PAL that "kind of" keeps it on track.)  Every time the internal music clock
(1)  598/     14C :                     	; overflows, it will update.  So a tempo of 80h will update every other
(1)  599/     14C :                     	; frame, or 30 times a second.
